<title>UK: Clyde &quot;delighted&quot; at shareholder support.</title>
<headline>Clyde &quot;delighted&quot; at shareholder support.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bid target Clyde Petroleum Plc said on Monday that it was &quot;delighted&quot; at shareholder support for the group's management and again urged shareholders to reject the offer from Gulf Canada Resources Ltd.</p>
<p>On Friday Gulf Canada said it had received acceptances in respect of just 0.02 percent of Clyde's issued share capital.</p>
<p>Gulf has extended its 432 million pound hostile bid launched in December last year to January 24.</p>
<p>&quot;I expected the level of Gulf Canada's acceptances to be inconsequential and am delighted our shareholders have shown their support for Clyde's management,&quot; said Clyde chairman Malcolm Gourlay.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
